+# ACOS v1.2 — Internal Consistency Audit
+
+**Run 2026-09-03, after all v1.2 edits, before packaging.** Mechanical where mechanisable, by inspection where not. This is a self-check on the v1.2 package, not an independent review, and it is labelled as such.
+
+---
+
+## 1. The twenty-condition gate
+
+Every condition was evaluated by script over the full artifact tree (`deliverables/*.md`, root `phase2-v1.2-*.md`, `analysis/*.md`).
+
+| # | Condition | Result |
+|---|---|---|
+| C1 | All 22 BLOCKING finding ids are cited at least twice (ledger plus at least one artifact) | **PASS** |
+| C2 | `SR-B2` appears only in the typo note; it is not propagated as a finding | **PASS** |
+| C3 | 22 verification cases VC-C1..C4, VC-S1..S4, VC-A1..A6, VC-L1..L4, VC-R1..R4 present in `36` | **PASS** |
+| C4 | Every numbered deliverable declares v1.2 in its version line | **PASS** |
+| C5 | `MAL_total` signature basis stated as **$756.00** consistently | **PASS** |
+| C6 | `Standing(month)` 31-day stated as **$186.00** consistently | **PASS** |
+| C7 | The v1.2 verdict is READY FOR NARROW THIRD RED TEAM; no artifact asserts implementation readiness | **PASS** |
+| C8 | Control-artifact count stated as 23 rows / 21 signed classes / 1 prohibition | **PASS** |
+| C9 | All six `value_direction` values enumerated identically wherever the taxonomy appears | **PASS** |
+| C10 | P8 is defined, cited in the property table and cited in the hand proof | **PASS** |
+| C11 | Five `StandingAuthorization` states used consistently | **PASS** |
+| C12 | Seven `Approval` states used consistently | **PASS** |
+| C13 | `ACOS-JCS-1` is named as control-artifact class 20 | **PASS** |
+| C14 | Attestation cadence stated as 5 minutes with k=3, in one place, cited elsewhere | **PASS** |
+| C15 | The mirror dispatch rule is an ordered first-match list, not a row set | **PASS** |
+| C16 | Fixture F2 present in `51`, exercising both `min()` directions | **PASS** |
+| C17 | Seven exclusions from `MAL_total`, consistently counted | **PASS** |
+| C18 | The independent recompute oracle is referenced from the artifacts that depend on it | **PASS** |
+| C19 | The SR-S4 deviation from `57`'s specified formula is flagged and routed to a third-review question | **PASS** |
+| C20 | Exactly one copy of the limits fixture exists; the root path is a pointer | **PASS** |
+
+## 2. Invariant resolution and the C5b entailment check
+
+**Resolution (mechanical).** Every `I\d+[a-f]?` identifier appearing in any deliverable resolves to a row in `phase2-v1.2-invariant-registry.md`. **Unresolved: zero.** All seventeen new identifiers — `I17e`, `I17f`, `I18a`–`I18d`, `I51`–`I61` — are cited in at least three deliverables each. `I18` appears only in historical passages explaining its retirement.
+
+**Entailment (C5b, new in v1.2).** Resolution is not enough: v1.1 passed a resolution check while citing `I31` for a property `I31` does not state. C5b asks, per citation, whether the cited invariant *entails* the property claimed at the citation site.
+
+**Four drifted citations found and corrected**, all the same drift — attributing verify-mode non-increase, or reservation absence, to `I31`'s uniqueness constraint:
+
+| Site | v1.1 citation | Corrected to |
+|---|---|---|
+| `22 §3` (R9 addition) | *"never re-taken and never topped up (I31)"* | `I31` for non-re-taking, **`I51`** for non-increase — two properties, two invariants |
+| `35 §4` | *"denies if it does not (I31)"* | **`I51`**, plus the `RESERVATION_ABSENT` denial for the absent case |
+| `36 §2` | *"(I31), and resume in verify mode never tops up"* | Split into two asserted properties; VC-R4 requires them to fail independently |
+| `48 §5.1` | *"refused if the reservation has been released or has expired (I31)"* | **`RESERVATION_ABSENT`** — `I31` says nothing about an absent reservation |
+
+The fourth is the most instructive: `I31` was cited for the *opposite* of what it states. A uniqueness constraint on `authorisation_id` guarantees a reservation is not duplicated; it cannot guarantee one exists.
+
+## 3. Arithmetic
+
+Recomputed independently by `analysis/recompute-v1.2.py`, which was written from `26 §10.1` and `51 §2` without reference to the printed figures — the condition `I7` actually requires and the one `54 §2.3` records v1.1 as failing, since that reviewer reproduced $300.00 only by inferring an unstated convention from the answer.
+
+| Quantity | Value |
+|---|---|
+| `MAL_monetary(month)` | $300.00 |
+| `Standing(month)`, 28/29/30-day | $182.40 |
+| `Standing(month)`, 31-day | $186.00 |
+| `MIE_cost(month)` p50 / p95 | $120.00 / $270.00 |
+| **`MAL_total(month)` p95, 31-day — signature basis** | **$756.00** |
+| `MAL_total(day)` p95 | $329.50 |
+| Realisable cash exposure | $906.00 |
+| F2 `MAL_monetary` | $480.00 = `min($300, $510)` + `min(UNBOUNDED, $180)` |
+
+Oracle output: `analysis/recompute-v1.2-output.txt`. **No arithmetic discrepancy found between the oracle and any artifact.**
+
+## 4. What this audit does not establish
+
+Stated because a passing self-check is the easiest thing in the package to over-read.
+
+1. **It does not establish that the twenty-two remediations are correct.** It establishes that they are consistently *stated*. `54 §2.1` reproduced every v1.1 figure correctly and v1.1 still contained 22 BLOCKING defects, all semantic.
+2. **It does not establish that the mechanical conditions are the right conditions.** They were chosen by the same process that produced the artifacts.
+3. **It does not exercise the two mechanisms the third review is scoped to.** Neither the inverted mirror machine nor the standing state machine can be validated by a consistency pass; both are adversarial questions.
+4. **C5b was run against the invariant citations, not against every cross-reference.** A `§`-reference pointing at the wrong section would not be caught. Section references were spot-checked, not exhaustively verified.
+5. **The SR-S4 deviation is flagged, not validated.** The exposure-remainder form defeats the constructed attack that `57`'s specified form does not; whether it opens a different one is a question for the third review, not for this pass.
+
+---
+
+**Gate result: 20 of 20 mechanical conditions pass. C5b found and corrected four drifted citations. No unresolved identifiers. No arithmetic discrepancies.**
